{"kind":"request","text":"MVP S3: questions with requested approvers, people only\n\nScope: the MVP plan's S3 (notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md, section S3), placed by plan 032 section 2b and filed now that S2 is promised (46b4a8fb), under sequencing ruling 261004b1. A data slice: a revision of the issue lane that uses only the guard forms the change lane already has (requests, and verdicts bound to a version). Build it as a declared successor of the current issue definition the way issue4.ts succeeds issue.ts: old bytes stay in place, the new definition is exported from apps/room/lanes/src/index.ts, and its pinned digest joins the table in docs/lanes-reference.md.\n\nDeliver, per the plan: ask gains body (detached, 64 KiB) and bodyAt (the entry that set the current text) and drops the single addressee; new acts revise-ask, request-approval and withdraw-approval-request bound to bodyAt, approve (verdict and comment) and decide; approve under grant issue.approve, where the signer is the requested member of an open request, request and approval name the current bodyAt, and the approver is not the asker; decide under grant issue.decide, with no open request and no request-changes verdict on the current text and at least one approval; both grants to person roles only; comment gains about; release-block accepts decide. Size stays inside PROPOSED_BOUNDS (16 item types, 64 acts, packages/contract/src/bounds.ts).\n\nFiles: apps/room/lanes/src/issue-questions.ts (new), its pinned bytes beside the existing digests files, one scenario in apps/room/lanes/test/*.scope.test.ts, docs/lanes-reference.md. If S1 has landed when this head is ready, add the activation of the new issue definition to examples/repo-in-ai/runbook.md; the planner runs it in the S1 room.\n\nDone when, the plan's witnesses, each as an assertion in the scenario: a requested agent is refused approve and the requested person is accepted; an agent is refused decide and the owner is accepted; an unrequested member is refused; an approval of old text is refused after revise-ask; decide with an open request is refused; another question's decision is refused with not-this-ask.\n\nNot before: nothing beyond main; S2 runs alongside. S4 (Needs you, Work, Decision context) rests on this slice and is filed when S3 is promised. Checker approves the exact head; gate passes; no deployment unless the lane definitions are served by a Worker, in which case the planner deploys.","body":{"conditions":"Done when: the six plan witnesses pass as scenario assertions (requested agent refused approve, requested person accepted; agent refused decide, owner accepted; unrequested member refused; approval of old text refused after revise-ask; decide with an open request refused; another question's decision refused not-this-ask); pinned digest in docs/lanes-reference.md. Not before: nothing beyond main. Checker approves the exact head; gate passes.","target_head":"5dc9765fdc6fb6896b736127801944c46ee288f9","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}